cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PerfOracle in academic work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "PerfOracle: Predicting Algorithm Performance Across Programming Languages and Hardware, from Microcontrollers to Edge AI"
abstract: >-
  PerfOracle is a system that predicts the performance of unseen source code on a
  specified language runtime and hardware target. It combines an automated
  benchmark harness and measured multi-hardware dataset with a learned predictor
  that maps source code, language and a hardware descriptor to runtime, peak
  memory, empirical complexity, energy, estimated carbon emissions and
  fit-on-target probability.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: Apache-2.0
